Erik,

The first problem you reported is fixed in svn. Nothing to do with
SQLite performance (all the create and insert statements used to
make the db take less than 1s or 2s in total). The problem was
earlier with an internal helper function in charge of doing some
cleaning of the downloaded data (before they are actually sent to
the db).
makeTranscriptDbFromUCSC(genome="mm9", tablename="refGene") now takes
80s (vs 45 min before the fix).

I still need to look at this other problem you found. I'll let you
know.

H.


